/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear Linear interpolation
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Interpolation
 * @brief Map physical and normalized coordinates through a linear segment.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear_Goal Goal
 * Separate the coordinate system from the signal values: interpolate at a
 * physical point, intentionally extrapolate a normalized point, and observe
 * how a collapsed input axis selects its 0-side.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Interpolation_Linear_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Physical x=15 in [10,20]: value=5; expected=5
 * Normalized t=2: extrapolated=14; expected=14
 * Collapsed axis selects value0: PASS
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * Extrapolation is a deliberate linear continuation. A collapsed physical
 * axis maps to normalized zero, avoiding division by zero and selecting the
 * value at that axis' 0 endpoint.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear_Code Implementation
 * \include Interpolation/Linear/Shared.cpp
 */
